    "body": "**Summary**\r\n\r\nFix incomplete zero-copy memory registration for MLA host pools using the page_first_kv_split layout.\r\n\r\nThis layout allocates separate K, V, Indexer, and optional Indexer-scale buffers, but kv_buffer aliases only K. Without get_hybrid_pool_buffer(), Mooncake falls back to registering only K, while get_page_buffer_meta() also returns pointers into the other allocations. Accessing these unregistered buffers causes TRANSFER_FAIL errors and transfer timeouts with GLM-5.2 + HiCache + Mooncake on Ascend.\r\n\r\n**Changes**\r\n\r\nImplement MLATokenToKVPoolHost.get_hybrid_pool_buffer() to expose all non-None physical backing buffers for the split layout.\r\nPreserve single-buffer registration for ordinary layouts.\r\nAdd regression coverage for optional Indexer/scale buffers, FP8 storage, differing KV/Indexer layer counts, ordinary layouts, and dummy pools.\r\nVerify registration pointers and byte lengths, including coverage of every zero-copy page range.\r\n\r\n**Testing**\r\n\r\nAll four regression test methods passed on an NPU machine, including split-buffer registration, zero-copy page-range coverage, ordinary layouts, missing optional attributes, and dummy pools.\r\nValidated GLM-5.2 + HiCache + Mooncake in an actual NPU environment.\r\nConfirmed that removing the fix causes five regression scenarios to fail due to K-only registration.\r\nPassed Ruff lint and formatting, isort, Python syntax, and diff whitespace checks.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35952751634](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35952751634)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35952751389](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35952751389)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35952751796](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35952751796)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
